WEBVTT

00:06.589 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:46.004 --> 00:49.090
[sweet music playing]

00:51.009 --> 00:52.886
Let's forget this.

00:52.969 --> 00:54.637
No drama. Like adults.

00:54.721 --> 00:56.598
I hope things stay normal.

00:56.681 --> 00:59.434
No drama. Like adults.

00:59.517 --> 01:00.852
[awkward chuckle]

01:00.935 --> 01:03.021
- So…
- [sheets rustle]

01:07.567 --> 01:09.569
[upbeat music]

01:25.585 --> 01:27.253
[sighs]

01:27.337 --> 01:29.047
I've gone insane.

01:31.007 --> 01:32.300
[chuckles]

01:34.636 --> 01:36.095
[Si-woo] Are you hungry?

01:36.179 --> 01:37.931
Do you wanna grab something to… Oh!

01:56.783 --> 01:58.284
Ha-kyung's still not home?

01:59.494 --> 02:02.956
And what did she say
yesterday on the phone?

02:03.039 --> 02:07.001
She said, uh, don't you worry
'cause she will fight Han Ki-jun and win.

02:07.085 --> 02:08.711
[sighs]

02:10.588 --> 02:12.757
[door squeaks]

02:18.888 --> 02:20.348
[Tae-kyung] Hey! You…

02:20.431 --> 02:22.767
How about you give us a call
if you're not coming home?

02:22.851 --> 02:24.352
You know how worried Mom was?

02:25.895 --> 02:27.814
Where were you? Coming back from work?

02:29.107 --> 02:30.108
Uh-huh.

02:30.984 --> 02:33.069
- Breakfast?
- I'm not hungry.

02:35.029 --> 02:37.407
[door slides]

02:39.367 --> 02:40.994
She's not thinking about eating.

02:41.077 --> 02:42.662
I know the look on her face.

02:43.538 --> 02:45.206
It's a problem with closure.

02:46.249 --> 02:48.418
I know at heart she's a smart person.

02:48.501 --> 02:49.794
Only sometimes it feels like

02:49.878 --> 02:52.589
she can't take what she's owed
in life from anyone.

02:53.590 --> 02:54.924
[sighs]

02:55.008 --> 02:56.175
Wait a second.

03:06.519 --> 03:08.771
[groaning]

03:10.857 --> 03:13.818
[comical music]

03:18.615 --> 03:21.034
- Oh, no.
- She's crying?

03:22.577 --> 03:24.495
- Out of my way.
- Oh, no, Mom. Ma.

03:25.079 --> 03:26.414
[Tae-kyung] Let her be.

03:26.497 --> 03:27.624
You get it?

03:27.707 --> 03:30.877
She got a hole shot through her heart
from the dude that she was going to marry.

03:30.960 --> 03:33.713
That guy, that guy,
I knew he was a problem.

03:33.796 --> 03:35.590
The way she always made excuses.

03:35.673 --> 03:38.509
Yes, I know. And I'm sure
she's embarrassed right now.

03:38.593 --> 03:41.679
What's she embarrassed for, huh?
It fell apart because he wronged her.

03:41.763 --> 03:44.641
Mom, let's let her rest, huh?

03:44.724 --> 03:48.353
Let's just go and give her a chance
to think it through, huh?

03:48.436 --> 03:49.729
[sighs]

03:53.775 --> 03:56.361
[quirky music]

04:03.409 --> 04:05.620
[rips, clinks]

04:05.703 --> 04:07.163
[body thud]

04:09.874 --> 04:11.501
[sighs]

04:12.627 --> 04:13.711
I'm insane.

04:19.300 --> 04:20.343
[sneezes]

04:22.387 --> 04:24.055
[sniffles]

04:25.640 --> 04:27.267
[sighs]

04:27.350 --> 04:30.228
The yellow dust affecting air conditions
last night is gone.

04:30.311 --> 04:34.565
Overall, it will feel a little more
like early summer than a spring day today.

04:34.649 --> 04:38.319
Midday temperatures are set to reach
up to 28 degrees in Seoul.

04:38.403 --> 04:40.989
[forecaster]
Eight degrees higher than yesterday.

04:41.072 --> 04:43.074
[light music playing]

04:48.621 --> 04:50.456
[Si-woo] It's tough
when the season's changing.

04:53.251 --> 04:57.130
You don't know whether to wear
thick layers or thin.

04:58.673 --> 05:00.049
TRY A SUMMER DELICACY!

05:00.133 --> 05:01.676
- Bye. Thank you.
- Thank you.

05:01.759 --> 05:03.553
COLD BUCKWHEAT NOODLES
SPICY BUCKWHEAT NOODLES

05:03.636 --> 05:05.179
[slurps]

05:05.263 --> 05:08.725
- Eat hot food or cold.
- Yes. Mm-hmm.

05:09.517 --> 05:10.810
- Hello.
- Hello.

05:16.107 --> 05:17.734
- Uh, hot, uh…
- [steam hisses]

05:17.817 --> 05:19.652
Uh, no, uh, iced Americano, please.

05:19.736 --> 05:20.987
- Just one?
- [Si-woo] Yeah.

05:21.070 --> 05:22.530
- Okay.
- [Si-woo] Thank you.

05:22.613 --> 05:24.032
[coffee machine clanks]

05:33.333 --> 05:38.171
[Si-woo] That's why sometimes I can't tell
if this feeling I'm feeling

05:38.254 --> 05:40.965
is sorrow for the season
I'm leaving behind

05:41.049 --> 05:44.969
or excitement for the season soon to come.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.638
- [dings]
- [automated voice] Please walk.

05:50.892 --> 05:54.479
[Si-woo] But one thing's for sure.
Summer's almost here.

05:57.398 --> 05:59.442
[traffic light beeps]

06:00.109 --> 06:02.111
[phone buzzes]

06:10.369 --> 06:13.748
[buzzing continues]

06:16.417 --> 06:17.710
[sneezes]

06:25.426 --> 06:31.057
EPISODE 3
IN BETWEEN SEASONS

06:31.140 --> 06:33.142
[gentle music]

06:41.359 --> 06:42.860
[sighs]

07:10.471 --> 07:13.641
[Ki-jun] Leaving for work.
I made breakfast. Eat before you leave.

07:15.309 --> 07:16.686
[chuckles]

07:23.109 --> 07:24.986
[munches]

07:27.697 --> 07:28.698
Hmm?

07:36.122 --> 07:38.332
- [Dong-han sighs]
- [door opens]

07:40.501 --> 07:42.545
Oh, off to school?

07:43.296 --> 07:44.297
[sighs]

07:44.380 --> 07:45.798
See you later.

07:45.882 --> 07:48.134
[Hyang-rae] Call me
when your afterschool classes are over.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.552
- [Bo-mi] Okay.
- Ah, have a good day.

07:51.721 --> 07:53.014
[door lock beeps]

07:53.097 --> 07:55.808
What's with her?
Is she always sour in the morning?

07:55.892 --> 07:59.353
You can't just walk around like that
in front of your grownup daughter.

08:00.396 --> 08:01.439
Oh…

08:01.522 --> 08:03.774
Why? I am her father.

08:04.650 --> 08:09.780
Yeah. I suppose so, but she hasn't lived
with you for over 14 years.

08:17.830 --> 08:19.081
[Soo-ja] Breakfast is ready.

08:19.165 --> 08:20.416
At least have a little, huh?

08:20.500 --> 08:21.459
I'm late.

08:25.213 --> 08:28.841
Your car isn't out front.
Where is it, at work or uh…

08:28.925 --> 08:30.009
[gasps]

08:30.092 --> 08:32.094
[quirky music]

08:32.970 --> 08:34.472
- [bag thuds]
- Oh!

08:35.223 --> 08:36.224
[groans]

08:37.683 --> 08:39.727
[objects clattering]

08:39.810 --> 08:41.270
[hurried footsteps]

08:42.396 --> 08:44.732
Ah, it's fine.

08:44.815 --> 08:45.650
See you later.

08:47.401 --> 08:49.695
[softly]
My gosh, this is insane.

08:49.779 --> 08:51.531
[door opens]

08:51.614 --> 08:52.740
Yes.

08:54.450 --> 08:57.286
No. We didn't find any car keys anywhere.

08:57.870 --> 08:58.788
Really?

08:58.871 --> 09:01.165
Can you check one more time?
'Cause I wanna be really sure.

09:01.249 --> 09:02.792
[Ha-kyung] Yes. Thank you.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.048
[doors clank]

09:10.466 --> 09:11.717
Oh, yes.

09:12.885 --> 09:15.596
Um, the last seven days of buoy report.

09:15.680 --> 09:17.848
BUOY: EQUIPMENT USED
TO OBSERVE WEATHER CONDITIONS AT SEA

09:17.932 --> 09:20.393
Oh, they were in already.
Well, okay, thanks.

09:26.774 --> 09:28.109
[sneezes]

09:28.859 --> 09:31.195
- [Myung-ju] Sounds like you've got a cold.
- Yeah.

09:31.279 --> 09:33.489
Mm-hmm. You should be careful.

09:34.240 --> 09:35.908
[Seok-ho] Did you sleep in the cold?

09:36.993 --> 09:37.994
No.

09:38.661 --> 09:42.123
[dreamy music]

09:48.212 --> 09:49.922
No.
[chuckles]

09:50.923 --> 09:53.259
Did you… stay out last night?

09:53.342 --> 09:54.552
[Myung-ju] You wore that yesterday.

09:57.388 --> 09:58.931
You didn't go home?

10:00.808 --> 10:02.310
That's not important.

10:02.393 --> 10:04.979
[Myung-ju] Ooh, how intriguing,
Forecaster.

10:05.062 --> 10:06.647
[sucks teeth]
You're a fascinating guy.

10:06.731 --> 10:08.608
Ooh…

10:08.691 --> 10:09.942
[Si-woo chuckles]
It's not that.

10:10.026 --> 10:12.028
I haven't found a new home,
so I've been staying over

10:12.111 --> 10:13.613
at the new training center.

10:13.696 --> 10:16.657
But, uh, I have to be out of there
before the month's over.

10:16.741 --> 10:18.284
So my stuff's all sealed up.

10:18.951 --> 10:20.328
[Myung-ju] I see.

10:20.411 --> 10:23.164
Oh, Shin, don't you have a spare room?

10:23.748 --> 10:25.958
Didn't you win
an apartment voucher last year?

10:27.793 --> 10:28.628
Did you?

10:29.503 --> 10:31.631
It's not mine, really. It's the bank's.

10:31.714 --> 10:34.675
Hey, I'm not asking to stay for free.
I'd pay fair rent.

10:34.759 --> 10:37.303
Si-woo, I'm not the type
who can live with another person.

10:38.804 --> 10:41.682
Where is Director Jin?
Is she always this late?

10:43.893 --> 10:45.353
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:48.939 --> 10:50.149
[Seok-ho] That's strange.

10:50.232 --> 10:51.859
She's never been late before.

10:57.281 --> 10:59.700
[vehicles honking]

11:09.043 --> 11:12.129
[funky music]

11:21.514 --> 11:23.891
[Soo-jin] Director, where are you?
We're starting the meeting.

11:24.850 --> 11:26.352
[Ha-kyung] There's a lot of traffic.

11:27.937 --> 11:30.648
Let Senior Forecaster Um open the meeting.

11:32.525 --> 11:34.443
[sighs]

11:41.409 --> 11:43.202
Director Jin is running a little late.

11:43.285 --> 11:45.371
She said you should open
the meeting and start it.

11:49.125 --> 11:50.292
All right. Good morning.

11:50.960 --> 11:52.962
All right, all right. Hey.

11:57.591 --> 11:59.385
[clears throat]

12:02.263 --> 12:05.266
[brakes squeal]

12:05.349 --> 12:07.393
KMA BUS STOP

12:19.822 --> 12:21.615
[sighs]

12:22.825 --> 12:24.076
You're all right. Sit.

12:25.494 --> 12:28.205
- Has it started?
- She's not even here yet.

12:28.289 --> 12:29.457
She's not here?

12:32.626 --> 12:35.087
[Myung-ju] Soo-jin, did you tell him?

12:40.259 --> 12:42.928
[pencil clacking]

12:49.727 --> 12:52.396
[funky music]

13:02.698 --> 13:03.991
[Myung-ju] Where is Director Jin?

13:04.742 --> 13:06.994
[Soo-jin] She's not
even reading my messages anymore.

13:09.872 --> 13:12.041
[Myung-ju] Ask Senior Forecaster Um
to start the meeting.

13:12.124 --> 13:14.293
[Soo-jin] I told him twice already.

13:16.170 --> 13:17.630
But he isn't doing anything.

13:21.342 --> 13:23.844
[Seok-ho] Senior Forecaster Um,
you should start the meeting.

13:23.928 --> 13:25.679
[phone buzzes]

13:27.681 --> 13:28.891
[softly]
Mr. Um.

13:40.069 --> 13:41.445
[sighs]

13:44.865 --> 13:46.408
[heels clacking]

13:47.368 --> 13:50.287
[coughs, pants]
I'm sorry.

13:50.371 --> 13:52.248
[Ha-kyung heaving]
I left my car here last night…

13:52.331 --> 13:54.375
Okay, whatever. Let's get started.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.584
I'm sorry.

13:58.712 --> 14:00.631
[Ha-kyung panting]

14:03.092 --> 14:05.553
- [gaps]
- [clacks]

14:07.179 --> 14:08.180
[Ha-kyung] I'm sorry.

14:14.144 --> 14:15.813
[objects clattering]

14:19.900 --> 14:20.859
Can we start?

14:21.527 --> 14:22.611
Yes.

14:27.157 --> 14:29.577
We will now call to order
our meeting for May 10th.

14:29.660 --> 14:32.204
Okay, satellite--
[sneezes]

14:32.288 --> 14:34.957
[comical music]

14:37.376 --> 14:38.460
[panting]

14:39.587 --> 14:41.672
I apol… apologize.

14:41.755 --> 14:43.799
Please report, Satellite Center.

14:43.883 --> 14:47.011
[man] Wind speeds are high
at the edge of the southern anticyclone,

14:47.094 --> 14:49.430
so we've put out a wind advisory
for the West Sea.

14:51.932 --> 14:53.017
Um, if you, uh…

14:53.100 --> 14:55.060
Thank… thank you very much.

14:56.562 --> 14:58.105
- [tissues rustling]
- [Ha-kyung sniffles]

15:01.025 --> 15:02.610
[sighs]

15:02.693 --> 15:04.361
If you look at the satellite image,

15:04.445 --> 15:06.614
you can see that the clouds
are rotating clockwise

15:06.697 --> 15:08.657
with Gyeongbuk Province at the center.

15:08.741 --> 15:11.452
- Under such circumstances, the--
- [man] Uh, no, no. Hold on.

15:11.535 --> 15:12.578
First, we need a briefing

15:12.661 --> 15:15.247
on the wind advisory situation
from two days ago.

15:15.748 --> 15:17.082
Sorry?

15:17.166 --> 15:20.210
It's chaos here
because of the high wind advisory.

15:20.294 --> 15:22.296
[pensive music]

15:24.089 --> 15:27.676
How can you keep the fishing ban?
This is our livelihood you're destroying.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.011
Last year's campaign,

15:29.094 --> 15:31.931
you said you'd make things better
for the fishermen, is this better, huh?

15:32.014 --> 15:34.058
You know crabs only have
a two-week season.

15:34.141 --> 15:36.936
And it's been two days since you've
banned us going there on our boats.

15:37.019 --> 15:38.228
We can't make a living, huh!

15:38.312 --> 15:40.981
Hey, come on! Do you know anybody
in the Coast Guard?

15:41.065 --> 15:43.817
Get the Governor or something
and do something about this situation.

15:43.901 --> 15:45.402
- Come on, man.
- Do it!

15:45.486 --> 15:46.320
Absolutely not.

15:46.403 --> 15:47.529
COAST GUARD
SENIOR SUPERINTENDENT YOO WON-CHEOL

15:47.613 --> 15:49.531
I am fully aware of the fishing situation.

15:49.615 --> 15:51.951
You can't sail
until the Meteorology Administration

15:52.034 --> 15:53.285
lowers its advisory.

15:54.119 --> 15:57.122
Uh, we only have
nine patrol boats available.

15:57.748 --> 15:59.917
And our team here
and the Coast Guard's team

16:00.000 --> 16:01.919
is only 32 people total.

16:02.002 --> 16:04.964
Now imagine if there's some sort
of accident off the coast.

16:05.047 --> 16:06.757
I can't risk that happening!

16:07.466 --> 16:10.302
[taps]
I said I can't! And that's the end of it.

16:10.386 --> 16:11.345
[phone clacks]

16:11.428 --> 16:12.596
GWANGJU REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

16:12.680 --> 16:15.891
This is happening right now.
Shouldn't you do something about it?

16:15.975 --> 16:17.726
Um, sea conditions in that area are…

16:19.645 --> 16:21.146
[key clacks]

16:23.148 --> 16:24.441
[digital trill]

16:24.525 --> 16:28.237
The current wave, uh, wave period
on the West Coast

16:28.320 --> 16:30.823
is down to 11.4 seconds.

16:30.906 --> 16:33.784
Uh, also, if you look
at other ocean readings…

16:34.410 --> 16:35.369
Uh, well, I…

16:35.953 --> 16:37.121
Let's help her out.

16:37.705 --> 16:39.206
Send the summary to her.

16:41.959 --> 16:43.252
Mm…

16:45.045 --> 16:47.339
[pensive music]

16:52.761 --> 16:54.138
[Ha-kyung in shaky voice]
I'm sorry.

16:55.973 --> 16:59.893
I'm so sorry. I haven't completely
analyzed the situation.

17:03.230 --> 17:06.233
Senior Forecaster Um,
could you please take over for me?

17:07.234 --> 17:08.527
[inhales deeply]

17:09.153 --> 17:12.573
[exhales]
The wave height is still unstable.

17:12.656 --> 17:16.035
Considering the fact that
there's also long wind drift distance,

17:16.702 --> 17:19.329
it doesn't appear very likely
that the wind will subside soon.

17:19.413 --> 17:20.748
[Bong-chan] No?

17:21.331 --> 17:24.668
[sighs]
Goodness gracious.

17:25.753 --> 17:29.006
Well, what does Mr. Lee think?

17:29.089 --> 17:31.675
The wave height is still high,
but the wave period has dropped

17:31.759 --> 17:34.011
from 14.5 to 11.4 seconds.

17:34.094 --> 17:35.304
The wind velocity is going down

17:35.387 --> 17:37.890
and there are fewer
large surface waves than before.

17:37.973 --> 17:40.350
So you don't agree with Mr. Um, then.

17:41.477 --> 17:42.436
I don't.

17:45.189 --> 17:46.648
[mouths]
What?

17:47.483 --> 17:49.651
[Bong-chan sighs]

17:49.735 --> 17:53.572
It's the Administrator. It sounds like
it's about the wind advisory in Taean.

17:54.907 --> 17:56.116
[groans]

17:56.200 --> 17:58.410
I think local government's
pushing back on this one.

17:58.494 --> 18:00.913
- Oh, no.
- It's a little complicated.

18:00.996 --> 18:02.873
Director Jin, what are we going to do?

18:04.625 --> 18:08.587
Clearly, Mr. Um and Mr. Lee disagrees,
so as director, you should decide.

18:10.339 --> 18:12.091
[beeping]

18:17.387 --> 18:19.598
Hey, Director.
[light knocks]

18:19.681 --> 18:21.183
We'll observe the situation

18:21.266 --> 18:23.143
and consider
the wave height report carefully.

18:23.227 --> 18:26.772
TIME SECTION: A PERIOD OF 3 HOURS
IN WHICH WEATHER DATA IS UPDATED

18:27.648 --> 18:29.024
[heavy sigh]

18:32.486 --> 18:33.529
[Bong-chan] Yeah?

18:33.612 --> 18:35.906
[sucks teeth]
All right.

18:35.989 --> 18:38.575
Okay. Well, we've decided
no changes for the time being.

18:38.659 --> 18:40.410
- Announce this.
- Right away.

18:41.411 --> 18:42.871
[Ha-kyung] Meeting is now adjourned.

18:42.955 --> 18:44.581
[Bong-chan sighs]

18:49.878 --> 18:51.004
I'm sorry, sir.

18:51.588 --> 18:53.757
About what? Being late, unprepared?

18:53.841 --> 18:56.009
Sorry, we need more time
to observe the data.

18:57.344 --> 18:59.471
If we need time, then we'll take it.
What's the matter?

19:00.472 --> 19:03.350
You're gonna get complaints
from all over the country.

19:04.434 --> 19:05.435
Look, Director.

19:06.019 --> 19:07.604
[Bong-chan] That's for me to handle.

19:07.688 --> 19:11.900
Your role should stay focused
on the weather and the team here.

19:13.068 --> 19:15.112
Right. I apologize.

19:16.155 --> 19:17.406
[chuckles]
Knock it off.

19:18.699 --> 19:19.867
Great job, everyone.

19:19.950 --> 19:21.618
- Thank you very much, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

19:22.494 --> 19:24.037
[clears throat]

19:30.252 --> 19:33.589
I definitely told him that
you wanted to start the meeting.

19:34.173 --> 19:35.841
I told him two times.

19:35.924 --> 19:37.551
[hurried footsteps]

19:40.762 --> 19:42.681
- Coffee run?
- [leader] Sure.

19:44.558 --> 19:46.643
[sighs]

19:53.066 --> 19:54.151
Are you okay?

19:54.234 --> 19:58.238
[Ha-kyung] Why? 'Cause I was late?
Unprepared? Or embarrassed myself?

19:58.322 --> 19:59.615
Because of your cold.

19:59.698 --> 20:01.366
[Si-woo] You're sneezing a lot.

20:03.035 --> 20:06.205
I have rhinitis.
It acts up between seasons.

20:18.342 --> 20:20.802
[sweet music]

20:28.018 --> 20:29.770
[keyboard clacking]

20:29.853 --> 20:31.563
[phone vibrates]

20:36.944 --> 20:38.111
[message alert tone plops]

20:38.195 --> 20:39.655
[buyer] I wanna buy this.

20:39.738 --> 20:44.117
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET
SELLING AN AIR PURIFIER

20:44.201 --> 20:45.410
Thirty.

20:48.330 --> 20:49.414
[Ha-kyung] Okay.

20:50.123 --> 20:51.625
[sneezes]

20:53.126 --> 20:54.461
[coughs]

21:07.849 --> 21:09.685
What? Why are you still here?

21:14.856 --> 21:16.191
[Si-woo] Haven't you heard?

21:16.275 --> 21:18.694
I've officially been assigned
to Headquarters.

21:19.236 --> 21:21.405
[sighs]
Why would they put you here?

21:21.488 --> 21:24.116
If you're so curious about it,
you can go ask HR.

21:24.199 --> 21:25.701
They handle all the personnel.

21:25.784 --> 21:26.868
[sighs]

21:26.952 --> 21:29.162
And you're okay with seeing me
in the hall around here all the time?

21:29.246 --> 21:30.163
Uh-huh.

21:30.247 --> 21:33.375
It was my dream to work at Headquarters.
I'm gonna do my very best.

21:33.458 --> 21:37.337
I lost you
because I worked too hard for it. Right?

21:38.213 --> 21:41.300
You really think that I dumped you
for that reason?

21:41.883 --> 21:42.843
Then what's the reason?

21:42.926 --> 21:45.637
Did you really not put it together
or are you just playing coy?

21:49.266 --> 21:50.475
[chuckles]

21:52.477 --> 21:54.062
It's not important, though.

21:54.146 --> 21:57.149
You'll follow your road, and so will I.

21:57.232 --> 21:59.318
- [scoffs]
- [footsteps]

22:00.986 --> 22:02.154
[Eun-ji] Chae!

22:02.654 --> 22:04.990
- [chuckling]
- As you were, Reporter Chae.

22:12.080 --> 22:15.292
- Who's that?
- A Weather Alert Forecaster

22:15.375 --> 22:16.960
for Team Two, he just transferred here.

22:17.044 --> 22:18.962
[Eun-ji] So how do you know him?

22:19.046 --> 22:22.049
We barely know each other.
I met him a few times on the job.

22:22.132 --> 22:24.092
Oh, I see.

22:24.176 --> 22:25.135
[Eun-ji chuckles]

22:26.678 --> 22:27.679
[phones ringing]

22:27.763 --> 22:30.098
COAST GUARD TELLS FISHERMEN
TO STAY ALERT FOR POSSIBLE ACCIDENTS

22:30.182 --> 22:31.683
STRONG WINDS EXPECTED ON THE WEST COAST

22:31.767 --> 22:32.809
REGULAR FERRY OPERATIONS SUSPENDED

22:32.893 --> 22:34.061
EXTRA CAUTION REQUIRED
FOR MARITIME ACCIDENTS

22:34.144 --> 22:36.855
Yes, the advisory
hasn't been lifted just yet.

22:36.938 --> 22:38.523
- Yes, that's right.
- Yes, I'm listening.

22:38.607 --> 22:41.777
Yes, we know that there
are difficulties with your operation.

22:41.860 --> 22:45.489
Still, there's enough wave activity
in the West Sea to warrant our concern.

22:45.572 --> 22:49.242
- Yes. The wave height is still…
- I know you're frustrated.

22:49.326 --> 22:50.660
[staff] We still have to be careful.

22:50.744 --> 22:52.454
We really wish
we could just lift the advisory.

22:52.537 --> 22:54.039
- Yeah.
- [Min-jun] Yes, I like crab too.

22:54.122 --> 22:56.500
Believe me. We put these procedures in
for your safety.

22:56.583 --> 22:58.168
[Min-jun] We create these guidelines…

22:58.251 --> 22:59.503
Yes, of course.

22:59.586 --> 23:02.547
- The… the forum?
- [woman] Okay.

23:03.131 --> 23:04.591
- Yes, I understand.
- [mouse scrolling]

23:04.674 --> 23:07.677
- Uh, yes. Just a minute. Thanks.
- [Ju-won] Yes, okay.

23:07.761 --> 23:08.929
The forum's lost it.

23:12.432 --> 23:15.769
We're all suffering because the KMA
is making a big stink over nothing.

23:15.852 --> 23:18.939
It's not the weather that's gonna kill us.
It's the awful administration!

23:19.022 --> 23:21.525
- [water splashes]
- [groans]

23:21.608 --> 23:24.569
Yeah, right!
There's no high winds around here.

23:24.653 --> 23:27.030
- They don't know our ocean.
- [sighs]

23:27.114 --> 23:29.366
[Ju-won] I'll let you know
as soon as anything changes.

23:30.117 --> 23:31.868
- Yeah, yes.
- Oh, yes, of course.

23:31.952 --> 23:33.495
For safety, okay?

23:34.204 --> 23:35.831
- [phone clacks]
- [sighs]

23:37.249 --> 23:38.625
[sighs]

23:39.334 --> 23:40.752
We can't go on like this.

23:41.503 --> 23:42.921
- Director Han.
- Yes?

23:43.004 --> 23:44.881
You have to go to the Chief Team

23:44.965 --> 23:47.092
and at least have them approve
a preliminary advisory.

23:47.676 --> 23:49.052
"Advisory"?

23:49.136 --> 23:51.471
Yeah, we have to put out some info
about these waves out there

23:51.555 --> 23:53.306
when we might lift the advisory.

23:53.390 --> 23:55.976
Otherwise, all we're gonna do today
is answer calls.

23:56.059 --> 23:57.477
I'll ask them, then.

23:58.061 --> 24:00.438
Assistant Director,
which team is in charge right now?

24:01.648 --> 24:02.816
Team Two right now, I believe.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.236
[comical dramatic music]

24:06.319 --> 24:07.696
Oh, man.

24:08.363 --> 24:10.949
Aren't you uncomfortable
seeing me every single day like this?

24:11.032 --> 24:12.534
Oh, is it hard for you to see me?

24:12.617 --> 24:14.411
It sounds like you're the one
who should go.

24:14.494 --> 24:17.038
I think you'd do great in Geneva,
you asshole.

24:17.122 --> 24:19.749
[Ha-kyung echoing]
Asshole!

24:24.045 --> 24:25.046
What is it?

24:26.006 --> 24:29.092
The high wind advisory issued
on the Central West Sea,

24:29.176 --> 24:32.012
- it's lasted 40 hours.
- And so?

24:32.095 --> 24:35.640
It would improve things if you provided us
with an estimated end time--

24:35.724 --> 24:37.976
Ah, you must not have heard
the meeting decision.

24:38.059 --> 24:39.811
Because of the dangerous state
of the surface waves,

24:39.895 --> 24:42.480
we can't go any lower
than our current state of wind advisory

24:42.564 --> 24:43.773
until we have more information.

24:43.857 --> 24:46.568
That's why we'd like to give
a preliminary update.

24:47.152 --> 24:50.030
About when the waves might calm down,
this afternoon, tomorrow morning?

24:50.113 --> 24:52.240
[Ha-kyung] The wave height value
is still unstable.

24:52.324 --> 24:55.619
I can't send out an expected advisory
end time just to go and revise it.

24:55.702 --> 24:57.746
Let's leave things as they are.

24:57.829 --> 24:59.581
[pages rustle]

25:02.292 --> 25:03.585
You can, though.

25:05.795 --> 25:08.089
[tense music]

25:08.173 --> 25:09.382
[Ha-kyung] What do you mean?

25:10.383 --> 25:11.384
[Ki-jun] You could send it.

25:11.468 --> 25:13.803
You're drawing things out
on purpose out of spite.

25:13.887 --> 25:15.889
You're trying to hurt me now, aren't you?

25:16.473 --> 25:17.682
[scoffs]

25:17.766 --> 25:21.478
Are you saying that I'm ruining
the crab fishermen's livelihood

25:21.561 --> 25:24.231
just to make things a little
inconvenient for you here?

25:24.314 --> 25:26.441
- Aren't you?
- Listen, Mr. Han Ki-jun!

25:26.524 --> 25:27.943
[Si-woo] I can help with this.

25:31.071 --> 25:33.823
I handle Severe Weather Alerts,
so I can talk about it with you.

25:35.742 --> 25:37.994
Do you know what it's like
over in our office right now?

25:38.078 --> 25:40.247
We can't work while we have
dozens of calls coming in all the time

25:40.330 --> 25:42.374
from local governments
mad about the boats.

25:42.457 --> 25:44.209
How can we take care
of any other business?

25:44.793 --> 25:48.088
Shouldn't the Spokesperson's Office
at least be able to do its job?

25:48.171 --> 25:49.256
What?

25:49.923 --> 25:50.882
"Its job"?

25:50.966 --> 25:53.009
Everyone on the Chief Team
is busy with the data.

25:53.593 --> 25:55.720
[Si-woo] All we're talking about
is this wind advisory.

25:55.804 --> 25:56.930
We didn't even have lunch.

25:57.013 --> 26:00.308
Everyone here is working their ass off
to make sure the reports are accurate.

26:00.392 --> 26:03.186
Handling complaint calls
is one of your most basic duties.

26:03.270 --> 26:04.729
Our entire staff's on a crunch,

26:04.813 --> 26:06.940
and you came over here
to complain you job is hard?

26:07.023 --> 26:08.984
That's why you came all the way over here?

26:10.694 --> 26:13.655
This isn't your place
or your concern, so back off.

26:14.656 --> 26:16.199
Well, I do the alerts, so--

26:16.283 --> 26:19.744
So what, huh? Just wait,
and I'll talk to your director.

26:20.495 --> 26:22.205
That's enough, Mr. Lee.

26:22.831 --> 26:23.915
[scoffs]

26:23.999 --> 26:25.917
Mr. Han, you should go back
to your office.

26:26.501 --> 26:27.335
Hmm?

26:28.461 --> 26:29.754
Um…

26:30.922 --> 26:33.049
Hey, I… I should go or…

26:33.133 --> 26:34.759
[yells]
When there's severe weather,

26:35.885 --> 26:38.930
lack of caution leads to death,
are you aware of that?

26:39.014 --> 26:42.809
It's not a situation anyone would
draw out for some sad revenge.

26:43.476 --> 26:46.479
So go back and wait for our forecast.

26:53.987 --> 26:55.363
[clears throat]

26:55.447 --> 26:58.742
- Well, that's still--
- Go! And stay out of here.

27:08.251 --> 27:09.711
[exhales]

27:15.759 --> 27:17.719
[chuckles]

27:18.887 --> 27:20.472
[sighs]

27:29.481 --> 27:30.357
Is she okay?

27:31.358 --> 27:32.233
Hmm?

27:32.984 --> 27:34.486
Ha-kyung, well, she, uh…

27:35.070 --> 27:37.822
She acts like she has
a few screws loose in her head.

27:38.490 --> 27:39.657
I get it, though.

27:39.741 --> 27:42.035
Going to work every day must be hell.

27:43.286 --> 27:46.456
It's rough enough that she has to see
that bastard Han Ki-jun's face

27:46.539 --> 27:50.668
all over there all the time,
but her co-workers know all about it.

27:50.752 --> 27:53.838
So all she can do is ignore him
and keep working.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.465
Would you be okay if you were her?

27:58.301 --> 27:59.928
What, Mom? What's going on?

28:01.346 --> 28:02.430
[line dials]

28:02.514 --> 28:03.973
[line ringing]

28:04.057 --> 28:05.392
Oh, Ha-kyung.

28:05.475 --> 28:07.602
Uh, if you're having trouble at work--

28:07.685 --> 28:08.853
I'm busy right now, Ma.

28:08.937 --> 28:10.522
Oh, okay.

28:14.192 --> 28:15.193
I told you, Ma.

28:15.276 --> 28:18.279
The best thing for us to do
is leave her alone.

28:18.363 --> 28:22.158
She sounded kind of unwell.
Oh, Ha-kyung's sick.

28:29.207 --> 28:31.000
[approaching footsteps]

28:38.091 --> 28:38.925
Here.

28:39.551 --> 28:40.760
I told you it's rhinitis.

28:40.844 --> 28:41.970
[spoon clanking]

28:42.053 --> 28:43.430
You're not as sharp as you look.

28:45.765 --> 28:46.683
[spoon clinks]

28:49.352 --> 28:50.645
You have a fever.

28:50.729 --> 28:53.314
[tender music]

28:55.984 --> 28:57.110
[Si-woo] Take one right now.

28:59.487 --> 29:01.614
[medicine rustling]

29:02.657 --> 29:03.867
What do you think you're doing?

29:03.950 --> 29:05.618
It's just part of the job.

29:05.702 --> 29:06.911
Sucking up to the director.

29:16.713 --> 29:20.258
Don't worry, though. I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

29:23.303 --> 29:24.554
Take it now, okay?

29:40.069 --> 29:42.405
[birds squawking]

29:42.489 --> 29:43.656
[captain 1] Oh, jeez.

29:44.657 --> 29:46.493
- [captain 2 sighs]
- [captain 3] Hey!

29:46.576 --> 29:49.245
[captain 2 tongue clicks]
Oh, wait a second, eh?

29:49.829 --> 29:51.623
Yeah. Hey?

29:53.208 --> 29:54.959
The ocean's peaceful right now.

29:56.252 --> 29:58.755
[captain 4] I could swim in it,
so we could definitely sail.

29:59.839 --> 30:00.924
Huh?

30:01.424 --> 30:03.468
Our sailors have gone to sea
more times in their life

30:03.551 --> 30:04.594
than they've gone to the bathroom.

30:04.677 --> 30:06.137
Uh, how far out?

30:06.846 --> 30:09.265
Yeah. How does it look to you right now?

30:10.391 --> 30:11.351
Oh, okay.

30:12.060 --> 30:13.603
Oh, and can you describe, uh,

30:13.686 --> 30:16.105
the shape of the clouds
and the wind pattern in detail?

30:17.065 --> 30:18.358
Yes. Uh-huh.

30:22.654 --> 30:24.280
I checked on the situation on the ground.

30:24.364 --> 30:27.075
There are surface waves along the coast,
but it gets calm far out.

30:27.158 --> 30:28.368
Who told you that?

30:28.451 --> 30:30.912
Captain I met
when I was on a weather ship.

30:30.995 --> 30:32.497
He knows the weather around
the coast of Taean

30:32.580 --> 30:33.706
as well as he knows his palm.

30:34.290 --> 30:37.126
Each year, around 18 boats
are capsized due to surface waves

30:37.210 --> 30:39.546
and in those accidents,
32 sailors have died,

30:39.629 --> 30:43.424
and they all would have said they know
the sea as well as they know their palms.

30:43.508 --> 30:45.385
The wind on the sea surface is weak.

30:45.468 --> 30:48.263
It is risky
with the elevated wave height out there.

30:48.847 --> 30:51.474
Still, Mr. Lee's correct.
The wind velocity is declining.

30:51.558 --> 30:52.559
[inhales]

30:52.642 --> 30:53.685
- It's true.
- If we at least

30:53.768 --> 30:57.146
lower the advisory to a warning,
the bigger ships could sail.

30:57.230 --> 31:00.859
Then, there would be less pressure on you
and on the fishermen too.

31:01.442 --> 31:02.694
If we let the big ones go,

31:02.777 --> 31:04.696
the small ones are going
to follow one by one.

31:04.779 --> 31:05.947
Do you think we can control it?

31:06.030 --> 31:08.783
No one can.
That's why the Coast Guard's worried.

31:09.367 --> 31:11.119
So you wanna maintain the advisory order?

31:13.913 --> 31:15.373
[sighs]

31:16.124 --> 31:17.709
What do you think?

31:18.418 --> 31:19.460
[lips smack]

31:19.544 --> 31:21.588
If you're on the fence with it,

31:22.589 --> 31:24.007
just follow the numbers.

31:26.634 --> 31:30.388
But it's crab season, and we can't ignore
the local fishermen's situation.

31:31.222 --> 31:34.475
[Dong-han] Or you go
with Forecaster Lee's gut feeling,

31:34.559 --> 31:36.728
and then reduce the alert.

31:37.812 --> 31:41.983
Who knows? Maybe the Dragon King
of the Sea will calm the waves.

31:43.985 --> 31:45.194
[sighs]

31:45.278 --> 31:47.155
You talk like you're not involved here.

31:49.532 --> 31:52.368
Well, in the end, I'm not the one
who has to make the decision.

31:52.452 --> 31:53.661
It's on your head.

31:54.287 --> 31:55.705
Ah.

31:55.788 --> 31:56.831
Okay.

31:59.709 --> 32:02.378
[pensive music]

32:17.226 --> 32:19.354
[phone dialing]

32:20.313 --> 32:21.731
[phone ringing]

32:21.814 --> 32:23.399
Spokesperson's Office, this is Ki-jun.

32:23.483 --> 32:24.692
This is the decision made

32:24.776 --> 32:27.403
by the Chief Forecaster's Team
at 3:23 p.m.

32:27.487 --> 32:28.488
[whispers]
Sir, sir.

32:28.571 --> 32:30.782
- It's the Chief Team.
- Are they lifting it?

32:30.865 --> 32:31.783
Okay.

32:32.492 --> 32:33.576
Yes, go ahead.

32:33.660 --> 32:36.788
The wind and wave height on the West Coast
is down to a warning level,

32:36.871 --> 32:38.706
but the deviation
of the significant wave height

32:38.790 --> 32:40.083
in that area is large,

32:40.166 --> 32:42.460
so until nine o'clock,
monitoring will continue,

32:42.543 --> 32:45.463
then we'll decide whether
to lift it or drop it to a warning.

32:45.546 --> 32:47.632
Uh, Director Jin. What are you saying?

32:48.216 --> 32:49.467
[line beeping]

32:49.550 --> 32:52.095
Chief Director. Direc… Director Jin!

32:53.805 --> 32:55.348
[sighs]

32:56.933 --> 32:57.809
Hmm?

32:57.892 --> 32:59.644
[phones ringing]

32:59.727 --> 33:01.437
[all groaning]

33:01.521 --> 33:04.023
- Phones will be on fire again.
- Yes, hello. Spokesperson's Office.

33:04.107 --> 33:06.234
[Min-jun chuckles]
Yes, yes.

33:06.317 --> 33:08.444
[Ju-won] Yes, hello.
This is the Media Interface Office.

33:08.528 --> 33:11.948
[Min-jun] Yes, it's been extended
just a little bit. I'm sorry.

33:12.031 --> 33:14.033
Okay, I'll send out the update
and memo right now.

33:14.117 --> 33:14.993
Okay.

33:16.035 --> 33:17.328
[sighs]

33:17.912 --> 33:19.747
I didn't expect your team
to be so conservative.

33:20.832 --> 33:23.876
I made the decision
based on data, so what's wrong?

33:23.960 --> 33:25.169
There's one more thing
you have to consider

33:25.253 --> 33:26.754
aside from the charts and reports.

33:27.547 --> 33:28.673
[Si-woo] Intuition.

33:28.756 --> 33:31.467
Okay? And I know
I almost always get it right.

33:31.551 --> 33:33.428
[papers clack]

33:33.511 --> 33:35.179
- Forecaster.
- [Si-woo] Yes?

33:37.098 --> 33:39.809
Our job is a science.
If you want to stay on my team,

33:39.892 --> 33:42.478
please base your theories only
on science from now on,

33:42.562 --> 33:43.646
not your intuition.

33:43.730 --> 33:44.981
Got it?

33:51.320 --> 33:53.656
From right now, two o'clock
to nine o'clock tonight,

33:53.740 --> 33:56.075
the high wind advisory
on the West coast will be sustained.

33:56.159 --> 33:58.244
- I'll send that now.
- [keyboard clacking]

34:02.040 --> 34:03.583
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:03.666 --> 34:04.876
SEND NOTICE?
YES

34:04.959 --> 34:05.918
THE NOTICE HAS BEEN SENT

34:06.002 --> 34:08.171
WEST SEA COAST GUARD STATION

34:09.672 --> 34:11.090
[notification alert tone]

34:12.925 --> 34:16.387
NOTICE
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:18.431 --> 34:20.141
APPLICABLE AREA
CENTRAL WEST SEA, EAST SEA

34:20.767 --> 34:23.186
[sighs, tongue clicks]

34:24.479 --> 34:26.522
[phone dialing]

34:27.648 --> 34:28.816
Seriously?

34:29.650 --> 34:32.028
[sighs]
Oh, really?

34:32.945 --> 34:33.863
Yeah?

34:34.614 --> 34:36.032
[groans]
Yeah.

34:36.866 --> 34:39.285
[sighs]
This weather alert's gonna kill us all.

34:39.368 --> 34:41.120
It's gonna bankrupt us all.

34:41.204 --> 34:43.247
All right, that's it.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.875
- No ships are setting sail today.
- [yelling angrily]

34:45.958 --> 34:47.376
- Again?
- Are you kidding?

34:47.460 --> 34:49.754
- The weather is getting even.
- Come on.

34:49.837 --> 34:51.839
- This is shit.
- I can't believe it.

34:58.513 --> 35:00.515
[indistinct PA announcement]

35:02.141 --> 35:04.018
Who will cook all this food?

35:04.977 --> 35:07.772
I won't make you do it,
so stop complaining.

35:07.855 --> 35:09.982
Go over to the seafood counter

35:10.066 --> 35:12.360
and ask them
when the loach is coming in, okay?

35:12.443 --> 35:14.153
You're making fish soup tonight?

35:14.237 --> 35:16.114
Ha-kyung can't even eat fish soup

35:16.197 --> 35:18.825
- cause her stomach's no good.
- And so?

35:18.908 --> 35:20.952
Oh, yeah.

35:21.035 --> 35:22.745
[groans]

35:22.829 --> 35:25.206
And fish soup at home takes way too long.

35:25.289 --> 35:27.875
You can order it online
and it will become fresh the next day.

35:27.959 --> 35:29.252
It's not right.

35:33.464 --> 35:35.591
GREEN ONIONS
2,790 WON

35:35.675 --> 35:37.343
[metal clanking]

35:37.426 --> 35:39.262
[gasps]
Oh, my gosh, is that really you?

35:39.929 --> 35:41.514
Soo-ja, hi.

35:41.597 --> 35:42.515
Mrs. Lee!

35:43.099 --> 35:44.976
Gosh, long time no see.

35:45.643 --> 35:48.062
Have you… Are you feeling all right?

35:48.146 --> 35:50.523
You haven't come to your exercise class.

35:51.607 --> 35:54.026
Well, my youngest daughter
just had a child.

35:54.110 --> 35:55.820
- [gasps]
- I was in the US for a few months,

35:55.903 --> 35:57.989
just to give them a hand.
[chuckles]

35:58.072 --> 36:00.616
Ah. Is it a girl or a…

36:01.200 --> 36:03.244
- A girl!
- Wow, that's great.

36:03.327 --> 36:05.621
Daughters are just so wonderful.

36:05.705 --> 36:07.582
Your younger daughter
just got married, yeah?

36:08.416 --> 36:11.961
I got the invitation,
and I felt so bad I couldn't be there.

36:12.044 --> 36:13.004
[Lee] Oh, wait a second.

36:13.087 --> 36:15.548
I can give you a gift for her.
Hold on a moment.

36:15.631 --> 36:17.758
Oh, no. No, no, no. It's all right.

36:18.593 --> 36:20.011
Now, come on.

36:20.094 --> 36:22.013
You gave so much
when my youngest had her wedding.

36:22.096 --> 36:24.599
No, no, I said, uh, no, no.

36:24.682 --> 36:26.767
- [chuckles]
- Uh…

36:28.144 --> 36:30.354
She's not married.

36:30.438 --> 36:31.355
Huh?

36:31.939 --> 36:35.234
- Well, they called off the wedding.
- Oh, why?

36:35.318 --> 36:37.612
You were bragging
about how he's some hotshot

36:37.695 --> 36:40.573
at the same office as her, and I…

36:40.656 --> 36:43.492
[softly]
You bragged about that jerk, Han Ki-jun?

36:43.576 --> 36:47.496
- Shut it.
- What happened? Did something go wrong?

36:47.580 --> 36:49.415
Uh, no, it's all right.

36:49.498 --> 36:52.668
It all happens, you know.
Divorces, too, or…

36:53.252 --> 36:57.757
I made them call it off
because he was wrong for her.

36:57.840 --> 36:59.383
Oh…

36:59.467 --> 37:02.178
I can't imagine how you must be feeling.

37:02.970 --> 37:04.764
Your older daughter got divorced

37:04.847 --> 37:07.767
and your youngest
lost her fiancé too, hmm?

37:08.392 --> 37:10.186
Did you hear? I told her to cancel it.

37:10.269 --> 37:13.522
I'm glad to see you're doing okay
after all you've been through, huh?

37:14.273 --> 37:16.108
I would have been so devastated.

37:16.192 --> 37:18.569
Aren't there worse things that can happen?

37:18.653 --> 37:22.657
And also, listen more carefully
when I'm talking to you, huh?

37:22.740 --> 37:26.410
My daughters, my girls,
they didn't get left, okay? They left.

37:26.494 --> 37:27.912
You, you tell her.

37:27.995 --> 37:31.582
- You divorced him, huh? Huh?
- Let's go, Ma.

37:31.666 --> 37:32.750
- Wait a second, okay?
- Later.

37:32.833 --> 37:35.878
- Why are you over here twisting my words?
- Mom, let's go.

37:36.671 --> 37:38.005
They have really good loach, okay?

37:38.089 --> 37:39.215
- They have it?
- They have it.

37:39.298 --> 37:41.300
- Let's go get it.
- Let's go. Let's just go.

37:50.601 --> 37:51.560
Goodbye.

37:52.228 --> 37:54.397
They opened a new Kalguksu
place near the office.

37:54.480 --> 37:56.065
Oh, sounds good. Sounds good.

37:56.732 --> 37:58.276
Uh, are you… are you, uh…

37:58.359 --> 38:00.152
Hmm, go on and enjoy yourselves.

38:00.236 --> 38:01.612
See you tomorrow, then.

38:02.113 --> 38:03.030
- All right.
- Let's go.

38:03.114 --> 38:04.865
- [Myung-ju] Is the place good?
- [Soo-jin] I heard it's great.

38:06.826 --> 38:08.119
Aren't you leaving?

38:08.202 --> 38:11.706
Oh, yeah. Oh, so stiff.

38:15.918 --> 38:16.961
Uh…

38:17.503 --> 38:19.839
- See you tomorrow, then.
- All right. See you tomorrow.

38:24.093 --> 38:25.886
- [Ha-kyung] Mr. Um.
- Huh?

38:27.138 --> 38:28.973
Don't you have something
to say to me right now?

38:29.056 --> 38:30.266
Um, not really.

38:33.686 --> 38:35.855
Why? Do you have something to say?

38:39.900 --> 38:44.363
It's okay if you don't like me,
but work is work, and…

38:45.114 --> 38:46.115
Of course.

38:46.741 --> 38:49.201
It's my fault I was late to our meeting.

38:49.285 --> 38:53.122
However, you still could have covered
for me at the start of it.

38:53.205 --> 38:54.373
Oh.

38:55.333 --> 38:57.335
Then you should have ordered me
to do that.

39:00.004 --> 39:02.923
Well, I know it can be uncomfortable

39:03.007 --> 39:06.010
to have someone who is so much
more experience as your subordinate.

39:06.093 --> 39:07.595
[Dong-han] I'm sure there's pressure.

39:07.678 --> 39:11.057
But when it comes to work,
you're my superior, and so,

39:11.140 --> 39:13.392
I'm gonna do what you say
that I should do.

39:15.227 --> 39:17.438
So don't be afraid to give me orders
when you need to.

39:19.774 --> 39:21.817
I know what it's like to be there.

39:21.901 --> 39:25.529
If you're not quick enough
on the draw, you get complaints.

39:26.322 --> 39:27.698
And if your call's controversial,

39:27.782 --> 39:30.242
you're always gonna have people
speaking out against you.

39:30.326 --> 39:33.579
And if you don't make the hard calls,
well, everyone ignores you.

39:35.456 --> 39:36.832
You know what I'm saying?

39:37.416 --> 39:38.751
Yeah, I get it.

39:40.127 --> 39:42.546
Even so, you'll still need time
to adjust here.

39:43.255 --> 39:44.340
I promise…

39:44.965 --> 39:46.425
to not be so late.

39:47.385 --> 39:49.637
However, if something
like that does happen again

39:49.720 --> 39:52.098
due to an unforeseen cause,

39:52.848 --> 39:55.768
come in where I would
and get everything going.

39:58.396 --> 39:59.730
That's a command.

40:01.148 --> 40:02.525
[chuckles]

40:02.608 --> 40:04.610
Yeah. See you tomorrow, then.

40:05.653 --> 40:06.779
[Ha-kyung] See you tomorrow.

40:11.158 --> 40:14.036
[breathes deeply]

40:24.338 --> 40:26.298
[phone buzzes]

40:30.386 --> 40:31.345
Yeah?

40:31.429 --> 40:33.806
[Tae-kyung] Ha-kyung,
you should come home late tonight.

40:34.849 --> 40:35.683
Why?

40:35.766 --> 40:39.186
Mrs. Bae started downing soju
and she's not stopping.

40:40.563 --> 40:43.858
- [glass clacks]
- [exhales]

40:46.944 --> 40:53.117
[singing in Korean]
♪ The one I loved so much ♪

40:53.200 --> 40:54.785
[chuckles]

40:54.869 --> 40:59.623
- ♪ I lost him♪
- Okay. I got it.

41:01.584 --> 41:02.835
[chuckles]

41:10.092 --> 41:11.677
- [phone vibrates]
- [sighs]

41:14.555 --> 41:17.433
[buyer] Hey, could I get 20,000 off
on the air purifier

41:17.516 --> 41:19.393
if I come pick it up myself?

41:20.352 --> 41:22.730
[Ha-kyung] Can you come
to this address tonight and take it?

41:23.397 --> 41:24.273
[buyer] Yeah.

41:25.941 --> 41:29.236
APARTMENT 1201, BUILDING 308,
7, SHINJEONG-RO, DONGJAK-GU

41:34.825 --> 41:36.285
[seat belt clicks]

41:37.620 --> 41:40.247
[engine starts]

41:42.458 --> 41:44.668
[urine trickling]

41:50.007 --> 41:51.467
- Whoa!
- What the…

41:51.550 --> 41:54.011
[groans]
Gross.

41:56.764 --> 41:57.806
[groans]

41:57.890 --> 41:59.183
PLEASE KNOCK

42:03.187 --> 42:04.688
[sighs]

42:04.772 --> 42:07.066
You know you don't live here
all by yourself, right?

42:07.149 --> 42:10.486
- Mm-hmm.
- Why didn't you lock the bathroom door?

42:11.237 --> 42:13.364
I'm not used to it yet.

42:13.447 --> 42:14.990
Oh, my god.

42:17.326 --> 42:18.244
[sighs]

42:26.502 --> 42:28.504
- Isn't this your home?
- Huh?

42:29.046 --> 42:30.589
Why are you just standing there?

42:38.681 --> 42:40.641
[knocks on door]

42:46.230 --> 42:48.357
- Here, have some fruit.
- Thanks.

42:53.237 --> 42:55.614
That had to have given you a startle.

42:56.490 --> 42:58.826
[chuckles]
Your dad is so silly, right?

43:00.077 --> 43:00.911
Where is he now?

43:03.747 --> 43:06.000
Please, you shouldn't be too hard
on your father.

43:07.042 --> 43:10.713
He just doesn't know some things yet.
He spent a lot of time away.

43:10.796 --> 43:12.172
If you could be kinder--

43:12.256 --> 43:14.675
- Neither do I.
- Huh?

43:16.260 --> 43:18.721
- [chopsticks clack]
- I don't know some things either.

43:21.348 --> 43:23.392
I've never lived with Dad before.

43:27.021 --> 43:29.023
[somber music]

43:40.492 --> 43:42.536
[sighs]

43:53.839 --> 43:55.007
[door closes]

43:55.090 --> 43:56.884
[groans]

44:09.980 --> 44:12.650
[exasperated sigh]
Seriously?

44:24.703 --> 44:28.040
[mellow music]

44:30.250 --> 44:33.295
I'M OFF TO WORK.
I MADE BREAKFAST SO MAKE SURE TO EAT!

44:35.506 --> 44:36.507
[sighs]

44:46.308 --> 44:47.726
[Eun-ji] Have you heard?

44:47.810 --> 44:51.146
That lady who is supposed
to marry Deputy Director Han?

44:51.230 --> 44:52.398
Hmm?

44:52.481 --> 44:54.983
She made a whole scene
in the office yesterday.

44:55.067 --> 44:57.945
She slapped Deputy Director Han
in front of all those people.

44:59.905 --> 45:01.156
Um…

45:01.240 --> 45:04.660
And promised she'd never give up
their apartment.

45:04.743 --> 45:06.537
[Eun-ji sighs, clicks tongue]

45:06.620 --> 45:07.579
[scoffs]

45:16.213 --> 45:17.798
[breathes deeply]

45:19.675 --> 45:20.884
[door beeps]

45:22.761 --> 45:24.888
[plastic rustling]

45:29.893 --> 45:32.187
[breathes deeply]

45:34.314 --> 45:35.649
You're home early.

45:35.732 --> 45:37.151
Sorry, I didn't clean up.

45:37.818 --> 45:39.862
I ran out of time before work.

45:41.530 --> 45:43.824
It must've been hard
putting everything away.

45:43.907 --> 45:45.117
- [chuckles]
- Yu-jin.

45:47.119 --> 45:50.831
I told you at least put your plates away
after you're done with them.

45:50.914 --> 45:52.583
I was busy, though. You understand.

45:52.666 --> 45:54.585
I told you, they breed fruit flies.

45:55.294 --> 45:59.214
Those were from the banana peel
that you threw away in the regular trash.

45:59.298 --> 46:01.091
- That was only once.
- It was not, though.

46:01.175 --> 46:02.134
I…

46:03.385 --> 46:06.221
[sighs]
Forget it. Okay?

46:06.305 --> 46:10.142
Okay. You cleaned up,
so I'll go take out the trash.

46:10.225 --> 46:12.644
[plastic crinkles]

46:14.813 --> 46:16.106
[clattering]

46:17.858 --> 46:19.359
[gasps]

46:19.443 --> 46:23.530
- Oh, no.
- Why can't you do anything right?

46:25.657 --> 46:27.993
What about you?
What have you done that's great?

46:28.076 --> 46:30.370
Me? Wha… What have I done wrong?

46:32.623 --> 46:33.832
[sighs]

46:33.916 --> 46:36.460
The apartment you had with that woman,
did you take care of it?

46:37.169 --> 46:38.754
No. No, you didn't, huh?

46:40.297 --> 46:41.590
How did you know that?

46:41.673 --> 46:43.675
Everyone at work
knows about her. Everyone.

46:44.343 --> 46:47.304
You know the rent's so high here
'cause it's a short-term lease, right?

46:47.387 --> 46:49.932
We were supposed to move out
as soon as you got your money, okay?

46:50.015 --> 46:53.560
When's that happening?
We have no idea what we're doing.

46:54.603 --> 46:55.896
You don't have to worry about it.

46:55.979 --> 46:59.191
Why? Didn't she say
she's holding on to it?

46:59.274 --> 47:02.236
[scoffs]
The nerve of that woman, I swear to you.

47:02.319 --> 47:05.531
You said half the apartment's yours.
Why can't you fight her or something?

47:06.823 --> 47:08.200
[sighs]

47:08.283 --> 47:11.161
It cost us 20 million won,
and you deposited 5.

47:11.245 --> 47:12.788
[Ha-kyung] I paid the rest on my own.

47:12.871 --> 47:16.542
And I also covered the deposit,
down payment, and the mortgage on my own.

47:17.251 --> 47:19.670
Uh, then what does that mean?

47:19.753 --> 47:22.464
Halvsies? You must be joking.

47:22.548 --> 47:24.508
That's low, even for you.

47:26.510 --> 47:30.889
Anyway, it's not good for either of us
if things get complicated at work.

47:31.431 --> 47:33.308
This is how it is.
That's all you have to know.

47:37.396 --> 47:38.480
[sighs]

47:49.741 --> 47:50.659
[Si-woo] Yu-jin.

47:52.995 --> 47:54.913
I told you not to do this kind of stuff.

47:54.997 --> 47:57.666
- I can just take it out on my way out.
- Just leave it.

47:58.292 --> 47:59.960
I don't want you getting your hands dirty.

48:00.043 --> 48:02.337
Pss. All right.

48:02.421 --> 48:04.423
[giggles]

48:14.349 --> 48:15.517
[sighs]

48:16.852 --> 48:18.020
[exhales deeply]

48:38.665 --> 48:40.542
I really used to love sitting here.

48:43.754 --> 48:45.505
[doorbell rings]

48:48.467 --> 48:49.551
[doorknob clanks]

48:51.553 --> 48:54.723
[playful music]

48:55.349 --> 48:57.225
Lee Si-woo, why are you here?

49:01.021 --> 49:03.357
Huh? This is the right place.

49:04.983 --> 49:07.319
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET

49:07.402 --> 49:08.945
Are you "issue"?

49:09.571 --> 49:11.156
Wait, and you're "jjin"?

49:13.408 --> 49:15.118
[sighs]

49:17.204 --> 49:18.830
[door closes]

49:18.914 --> 49:20.791
[door lock beeps]

49:31.218 --> 49:32.636
Don't look around.

49:34.262 --> 49:35.472
Oh, okay.

49:40.060 --> 49:41.061
This is it?

49:41.687 --> 49:42.813
Just go.

49:43.438 --> 49:45.565
You know why
I don't want to sell it to you.

49:47.359 --> 49:48.318
Yeah.

49:51.113 --> 49:52.155
[gasps]

49:52.239 --> 49:54.700
- You're throwing this out?
- Come on, just go.

49:58.620 --> 49:59.621
Okay.

50:07.045 --> 50:08.880
- Oh, Director.
- What now?

50:09.423 --> 50:12.050
Is this your first time
selling something online?

50:12.134 --> 50:13.009
Yeah.

50:13.093 --> 50:15.262
I mean, this air purifier.

50:15.345 --> 50:17.597
You said you've only
tried it once to test it.

50:17.681 --> 50:19.474
Then it's almost brand new,

50:19.558 --> 50:21.435
and it's the number one model
of this kind.

50:21.518 --> 50:23.562
You could easily get 400,000 won for it.

50:23.645 --> 50:25.981
Why would you ever wanna settle
for 300,000?

50:27.566 --> 50:29.401
And this speaker is a limited edition,

50:29.484 --> 50:31.695
so you can't find it anywhere,
not even overseas.

50:31.778 --> 50:33.238
- Really?
- Yes.

50:33.321 --> 50:36.408
If you sell it to an audiophile, you can
get more than the original asking price.

50:36.491 --> 50:39.828
But you're selling a top-end FB speaker
like this one for half-price.

50:39.911 --> 50:41.455
This is not a sale. It's a giveaway.

50:42.456 --> 50:43.290
What's FB?

50:43.373 --> 50:46.376
Full box. It's the item
in its original package.

50:46.460 --> 50:47.335
Oh.

50:48.170 --> 50:52.466
Oh! And also, these pictures
of the products you posted on here.

50:53.800 --> 50:55.969
There are lots of scams
on this sort of site.

50:57.012 --> 51:00.223
So you should write your username
and the date on a piece of paper like this

51:00.307 --> 51:01.349
and take a picture with it.

51:01.433 --> 51:02.684
So they know you're for real.

51:03.268 --> 51:04.603
- Hmm.
- [Si-woo] Like this.

51:04.686 --> 51:05.520
YOSE AUTHENTIC SPEAKER
MAY 10TH JJIN

51:05.604 --> 51:06.772
Like this right here.

51:06.855 --> 51:08.940
Yeah, post the picture here.

51:09.024 --> 51:11.026
- Now you upload? Okay.
- Username. Yes.

51:11.109 --> 51:13.111
Date here. "No haggling."

51:13.195 --> 51:15.739
- So this means it's already a bargain.
- Uh-huh. Mm-hmm.

51:16.281 --> 51:17.491
- FB.
- Mm-hmm.

51:18.158 --> 51:20.035
Overseas limited edition.

51:20.118 --> 51:22.329
- And shippable.
- "Ship…"

51:25.624 --> 51:28.794
[heart pounding]

51:32.547 --> 51:33.673
[Si-woo] Don't worry, though.

51:33.757 --> 51:35.592
I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

51:36.718 --> 51:37.803
Why?

51:39.513 --> 51:41.348
- Huh?
- Oh?

51:42.808 --> 51:44.893
What? Why?

51:45.519 --> 51:47.646
You were the one
that just asked me why, though.

51:47.729 --> 51:50.023
No, I… I didn't. I wouldn't just…

51:53.109 --> 51:55.570
- Did I, um, do something wrong?
- No.

51:56.238 --> 51:57.739
Why would you have?

51:58.865 --> 52:00.659
Why are you acting so nervous right now?

52:01.993 --> 52:03.370
I'm not nervous at all.

52:09.125 --> 52:10.460
What?
[chuckles]

52:13.338 --> 52:14.381
[phone buzzes]

52:15.882 --> 52:16.883
Oh, hey!

52:18.468 --> 52:19.845
- A buyer?
- Yeah!

52:19.928 --> 52:22.013
- Oh…
- Buying it right now.

52:22.681 --> 52:23.807
Oh, that's great.

52:27.602 --> 52:28.979
[customer] Thanks so much for this.

52:30.146 --> 52:31.231
Thank you.

52:34.276 --> 52:35.277
[car door opens]

52:39.197 --> 52:41.324
[engine revs]

52:46.413 --> 52:47.789
You were so helpful.

52:48.456 --> 52:50.292
Well, then you can buy me dinner.

52:52.043 --> 52:54.462
- What are you saying?
- I'm just hungry.

52:55.046 --> 52:56.214
Does it have to be more?

52:57.841 --> 52:58.884
No, of course.

52:59.467 --> 53:01.094
What would you like, Forecaster?

53:01.845 --> 53:03.889
[exhales]
I'm fine with anything.

53:04.973 --> 53:06.016
Let's go.

53:09.436 --> 53:11.438
[insects chirping]

53:16.318 --> 53:23.199
[Soo-ja singing in Korean]
♪ Pale pink skirt ♪

53:24.034 --> 53:30.332
♪ Fluttered in the spring wind ♪

53:31.124 --> 53:37.589
♪ While chewing
On my coat string as usual ♪

53:38.256 --> 53:44.804
♪ On the way to the village shrine
Where wild orchids bloom ♪

53:44.888 --> 53:48.892
♪ When flowers bloomed ♪

53:50.268 --> 53:53.021
[mellow music]

54:36.189 --> 54:38.483
[Ha-kyung] It's hard
when the season's changing.

54:38.566 --> 54:42.487
You can't really say
if it'll be cold or hot.

54:42.570 --> 54:46.741
But just like the summer heat
that comes after spring goes by,

54:47.450 --> 54:50.328
after this vague
and difficult period is over,

54:50.412 --> 54:54.165
flowers of a new season
will bloom before you know it.

54:56.459 --> 54:58.294
[server] Here's that special
that you ordered.

54:58.878 --> 55:00.880
[background chatter]

55:05.802 --> 55:07.178
[Si-woo exhales]

55:07.887 --> 55:09.806
You're selling your place too?
[crunching]

55:10.515 --> 55:11.558
Mm-hmm.

55:11.641 --> 55:14.102
- That's a shame.
- It is.

55:14.185 --> 55:15.770
I would just live there, if I were you.

55:16.396 --> 55:18.189
You wouldn't understand it, but--

55:18.273 --> 55:19.566
I think I do understand.

55:20.316 --> 55:22.485
Ah, yeah.

55:23.737 --> 55:26.614
Anyway, that place
has too many weird memories.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.283
I really just have to leave there.

55:28.366 --> 55:30.618
You can't just toss everything he touched.

55:30.702 --> 55:32.078
[Si-woo] What about your heart?

55:32.162 --> 55:34.497
You wouldn't wanna
just throw that away, would you?

55:34.581 --> 55:36.374
Just because somebody's been in there?

55:37.500 --> 55:39.169
Well, it will help me to let go of him.

55:40.628 --> 55:42.464
You'll have some regrets
either way, you know.

55:44.424 --> 55:46.634
It's not like you can just
turn back the clock.

55:46.718 --> 55:49.304
You don't mean anything
to that person any longer.

55:50.263 --> 55:53.600
So it feels unfair that you're the one
who has to suffer the loss.

55:59.147 --> 56:00.774
I was hoping you wouldn't go through that.

56:05.695 --> 56:06.863
You're concerned?

56:07.614 --> 56:10.325
Well, as someone
who went through it, don't.

56:10.909 --> 56:12.243
I'll be all right.

56:16.664 --> 56:17.791
Hey, your medicine.

56:18.458 --> 56:19.667
Eat your food.

56:20.668 --> 56:23.088
[heart pounding]

56:26.591 --> 56:30.386
♪ Under the cloudy sky, I saw you ♪

56:30.470 --> 56:32.305
♪ That is when our love began ♪

56:32.388 --> 56:33.515
What are you doing?

56:34.557 --> 56:37.018
Hmm, you took it.

56:39.896 --> 56:41.231
Your fever broke.

56:48.279 --> 56:52.158
[Ha-kyung] Like I said, it's hard
when the season is changing.

56:52.242 --> 56:54.744
- [door opens]
- [bell chimes]

56:55.537 --> 56:57.539
- Oh, how cool.
- [waitress] Welcome.

56:57.622 --> 56:58.456
[gasps]

56:58.540 --> 56:59.582
- [waitress] How many people?
- [Soo-jin] Three.

56:59.666 --> 57:01.334
- [waitress] Three? Just a second.
- What is it?

57:02.627 --> 57:04.045
Over there.

57:04.129 --> 57:06.131
[Seok-ho] I think that table's available.

57:06.214 --> 57:08.591
We'll show you to your table
after we finish cleaning it off.

57:08.675 --> 57:09.801
- But why are you hiding?
- Shh!

57:11.553 --> 57:12.804
What do we do?

57:13.388 --> 57:14.472
They can't see us.

57:14.556 --> 57:15.515
Doing what?

57:16.766 --> 57:19.185
Don't you get it?
This thing between you and me?

57:21.479 --> 57:23.189
[gasps]
They're gonna see us.

57:23.898 --> 57:25.442
[chuckles]

57:25.525 --> 57:27.026
Hey, where are you going?

57:27.110 --> 57:28.153
[groans]

57:28.987 --> 57:30.405
This can't be.

57:31.030 --> 57:32.657
- Just a moment.
- [Soo-jin] All right.

57:34.033 --> 57:35.535
- Oh?
- [Myung-ju] Oh!

57:36.035 --> 57:37.537
Hey, what are you guys doing here?

57:37.620 --> 57:39.581
Director Shin said the chicken here
is really good.

57:39.664 --> 57:40.957
What are you doing?

57:41.040 --> 57:44.169
Oh, someone I know said
the chicken was good,

57:44.252 --> 57:45.753
so, so we had a drink together.

57:47.505 --> 57:48.840
Oh, she's a friend?

57:50.884 --> 57:51.801
Oh!

57:54.888 --> 57:57.932
[sneaky music]

58:02.353 --> 58:03.897
Uh, never mind.

58:03.980 --> 58:05.565
I thought I saw someone I knew.

58:05.648 --> 58:08.359
- [fire roaring]
- [stove crackling]

58:13.031 --> 58:14.824
[chuckles]
Well…

58:14.908 --> 58:16.659
[nervous chuckle]

58:16.743 --> 58:19.120
[Seok-ho] Well, if your friend's
already gone, do you wanna join us?

58:19.204 --> 58:21.623
Uh, no, something came up, so…

58:22.207 --> 58:23.833
- Have a great time.
- Ah.

58:23.917 --> 58:25.293
- See you.
- [Soo-jin] Goodbye.

58:25.376 --> 58:26.794
All right.

58:28.713 --> 58:30.798
- [waitress] Follow me, please.
- [Myung-ju] Ah, thanks.

58:50.235 --> 58:51.069
[mouths]
Come here.

59:01.538 --> 59:02.580
[Ha-kyung] How'd it go?

59:02.664 --> 59:04.749
No one suspected us, did they?

59:06.376 --> 59:07.710
Or did they?

59:07.794 --> 59:09.295
What's going on?

59:10.171 --> 59:11.381
What do you mean?

59:11.464 --> 59:12.549
With us.

59:13.049 --> 59:14.801
Do we have something
to hide from the others?

59:16.219 --> 59:18.888
Uh, I'm just worried that us
being seen here

59:18.972 --> 59:21.099
would stir up a misunderstanding.

59:21.182 --> 59:25.812
Rumors about us or they would think
we're maybe dating or something.

59:29.315 --> 59:30.400
That was almost bad.

59:35.405 --> 59:36.698
Do you have feelings for me?

59:42.120 --> 59:43.204
No. Why?

59:43.288 --> 59:44.747
It seems like you do.

59:46.541 --> 59:49.002
Well, I don't.
[chuckles nervously]

59:54.632 --> 59:56.968
[warm music]

59:58.720 --> 01:00:00.096
Does it seem like it?

01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:05.393
You should know,
I don't just flirt around.

01:00:06.227 --> 01:00:08.354
No. I'm not just flirting.

01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:09.647
So let me date you.

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:12.442
What? What happened
to let's not date just 'cause we…

01:00:12.525 --> 01:00:16.863
I wouldn't want to
if I were the only one with feelings.

01:00:17.905 --> 01:00:20.158
[romantic music]

01:00:22.869 --> 01:00:25.204
If we both feel something, we date.

01:00:25.788 --> 01:00:27.206
If not, we don't.

01:00:31.169 --> 01:00:32.587
So which is it?

01:00:35.048 --> 01:00:38.051
What are, uh… we?

01:00:39.385 --> 01:00:42.347
["Melting" by CHEEZE playing]

01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:24.555
[Ha-kyung] It's true that the recent
collision on the expressway happened

01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:27.100
because the visibility
was low from the fog.

01:01:27.183 --> 01:01:29.852
Why is our country behind
at implementing fog advisories?

01:01:30.478 --> 01:01:33.106
Reporters should have
enough integrity, not to twist facts.

01:01:33.189 --> 01:01:35.191
[Ki-jun] You have to be ready
if you do stuff like that.

01:01:35.274 --> 01:01:36.275
Ha-kyung's smart.

01:01:36.359 --> 01:01:39.487
There's a reason she's the youngest
director the division's ever had.

01:01:39.570 --> 01:01:40.780
- I think we need--
- Without a full plan?

01:01:40.863 --> 01:01:42.323
[Soo-jin] I think she works here.

01:01:42.407 --> 01:01:45.034
- If not, why would she hide?
- [Ha-kyung] Thanks for this. You may go.

01:01:45.118 --> 01:01:48.037
What? She's messing with him, right?

01:01:48.121 --> 01:01:49.038
What? No, no! Hang up!

01:01:49.122 --> 01:01:49.997
Oh, Forecaster.

01:01:50.081 --> 01:01:52.375
[Ha-kyung] You need to find cases
from other countries that have fogs

01:01:52.458 --> 01:01:54.043
like we do, I need them in the morning.

01:01:54.127 --> 01:01:55.253
What is all this?

01:01:55.336 --> 01:01:56.295
I stayed up for you.

01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:57.255
[Ha-kyung sighs]

01:01:57.338 --> 01:01:59.132
[Ha-kyung] This office romance
will be the death of me.
